          #relative.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              As always in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+topos+theory"} higher topos theory
              %em base
              \. Here: over any
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} base (∞,1)-topos
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+algebraic+K-theory"} differential algebraic K-theory
              may be understood via cohesion over a base of ∞-stacks over a site of arithmetic schemes (see there).
            %p
              Over the canonical base
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
              = succeed "-topos" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %p
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-geometric+morphism"} (∞,1)-geometric morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo :
