                    \\stackrel{\overset{\Pi}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{\Disc}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma}{\longrightarrow}}}
                    \\infty Grpd
                    \\stackrel{\overset{Disc}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{\Gamma}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{coDisc}{\longrightarrow}}}
                    \\mathbf{H}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}
              ” is meant to be pronounced “flat”. The interpretation of these three functors is discussed in detail at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos+--+structures"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos – structures
          %p Sometimes it is desireable to add further axioms, such as the following.
          #PiecesHavePoints.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              We say that
              %strong pieces have points
              for an object
