          %h2#references References
          %h3#precursors Precursors
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category-theoretic
            definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
            was proposed by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"} Bill Lawvere
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
          %p
            The observation that the further left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} locally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
            defines an intrinsic notion of paths and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+homotopy+groups+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} geometric homotopy groups in an (∞,1)-topos
            was suggested by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Williamson"} Richard Williamson
          %p
            The observation that the further right adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi coDisc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coDisc
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} local (∞,1)-topos
            serves to characterize
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} concrete (∞,1)-sheaves
            was amplified by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Carchedi"} David Carchedi
          %p Some aspects of the discussion here are, more or less explicitly, in
          %ul#SimpsonTeleman
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Simpson"}> Carlos Simpson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %em
                deRham theorem for
                = succeed "-stacks" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~teleman/math/simpson.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            For instance something similar to the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-connected+%28infinity%2C1%29-site"} ∞-connected site
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid+in+a+locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} fundamental ∞-groupoid in a locally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
            is the content of section 2.16. The
            %a{:href => "#LieTheory"} infinitesimal path ∞-groupoid adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Red
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Π
                    %mi inf
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi inf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{Red} \dashv \mathbf{\Pi}_{inf} \dashv \mathbf{\flat}_{inf})
            is essentially discussed in section 3. The notion of geometric realization (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos%20--%20structures#Homotopy"} structures in a cohesive (∞,1)-topos – geometric realization
          %ul
            %li#Simpson
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Simpson"}> Carlos Simpson
              ,
              %em The topological realization of a simplicial presheaf
              , (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9609004"}> arXiv:q-alg/9609004
              ).
          %p
            But, more or less explicitly, the presentation of geometric realization of simplicial presheaves is much older, going back to Artin-Mazur. See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+homotopy+groups+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} geometric homotopy groups in an (∞,1)-topos
            for a detailed commented list of literature.
          %p
            A characterization of infinitesimal extensions and formal smoothness by adjoint functors (discussed at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+cohesion"} infinitesimal cohesion
          %ul
            %li#KontsevichRosenbergSpaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Rosenberg"} Alexander Rosenberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em Noncommutative spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preprints/send?bid=2331"} ps
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preprints/send?bid=2303"} dvi
          %p
            in the context of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Q-categories"} Q-categories
            \.
          %h3#on_cohesive_toposes_proper
            On cohesive
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p On the material presented here:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                , Section 3 of:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.7930"}> arXiv:1310.7930
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Proper+Orbifold+Cohomology"} Proper Orbifold Cohomology
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.01101"} arXiv:2008.01101
          %p
            A model in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+differential+geometry"} derived differential geometry
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luigi+Alfonsi"}> Luigi Alfonsi
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+A.+S.+Young"} Charles A. S. Young
              %em Towards non-perturbative BV-theory via derived differential cohesive geometry
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.15106"}> arXiv:2307.15106
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p exposition:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luigi+Alfonsi"}> Luigi Alfonsi
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Derived
                  = succeed "-plectic" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a{:href => "M-Theory+and+Mathematics#Alfonsi2023"} talk at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-Theory+and+Mathematics"} M-Theory and Mathematics
              (Jan 2023) &amp;lbrack;slides:
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Alfonsi-MTheoryAndMath2023.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O7pQkyqCiA4"} YT
          %h3#ReferencesInHoTT In homotopy type theory
          %p
            Expositions and discussion of the formalization of cohesion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              %em Axiomatic cohesion in HoTT
              (
              %a{:href => "http://homotopytypetheory.org/2011/11/02/axiomatic-cohesion-in-hott/"}> blog post
              )
          %p
            The corresponding
            = succeed "-code" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
          %ul
            %li#Shulman
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/mikeshulman/HoTT/tree/master/Coq/Subcategories"} HoTT/Coq/Subcategories
          %p A first formalization is described in
          %ul
            %li#SchreiberShulman2012
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Quantum+gauge+field+theory+in+Cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} Quantum gauge field theory in Cohesive homotopy type theory
              %strong 158
              (2014) 109-126 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1408.0054"}> arXiv:1408.0054
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.158.8"} doi:10.4204/EPTCS.158.8
          %p following
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              %em Internalizing the External, or The Joys of Codiscreteness
              (
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2011/11/internalizing_the_external_or.html"}> blog post
              )
          %p Another formalization is given in
          %ul
            %li#Shulman15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Brouwer’s fixed-point theorem in real-cohesive homotopy type theory
              %strong 28
              6 (2018) 856-941 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.07584"}> arXiv:1509.07584
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0960129517000147"} doi:10.1017/S0960129517000147
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} cohesive homotopy type theory
          %h3#generalization_to_fractured_toposes
            Generalization to fractured
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractured+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"}
              fractured
              = succeed "-topos" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            is a kind of “local” generalization of cohesion, which applies for instance in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+mathematics"} condensed mathematics
            (cf.
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+local+contractibility"} condensed local contractibility
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Qi+Zhu"}> Qi Zhu
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Fractured Structure on Condensed Anima
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://1429cecd-24a0-4223-8b7c-1ebf47aa12e2.filesusr.com/ugd/8e912a_fe1c2f8e90094d0fa065fb8129687963.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/QiZhu-FracturedCondensed.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p with exposition in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Qi+Zhu"}> Qi Zhu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fractured structure on condensed spaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://1429cecd-24a0-4223-8b7c-1ebf47aa12e2.filesusr.com/ugd/8e912a_8d2a90176ed14969a877e77ec1b787da.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/QiZhuFracturedCondensed.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nima+Rasekh"}> Nima Rasekh
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em What is a topological structure?
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://guests.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/rasekh/Condensed.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Rasekh-TopologicalStructure.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
